      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Other program services Part III line 31</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Alma Community Care had the privilege of providing professional mental health help with gospel-centered care to over 135 unique families in Greater Logan Heights. We offered 18 parenting seminars in English and Spanish on three local school campuses taught by licensed bilingual marriage and family therapists. One mother had this to say about the impact of our work: The seminars help me personally because they give me ideas that I have yet to know and show me and my family that there are different ways to approach issues. It also lets me know that my family isnt the only one going through our everyday life issues. Our parents reported learning a number of new skills like how to recognize mental health issues in their children and how to ask for help as well as how to analyze their own emotions and teach their kids how to deal with theirs. We also provided over 60 individual therapy sessions to nine community mothers and one father at no cost to them. One mother had this to say about her experience in therapy Therapy changed my mentality as a person. It helped me identify and modify limiting thoughts and beliefs. It also helped me improve the way I relate to others and overcome crises of silence. It helped me to be more expressive, that it is not good to remain silent, and that I should express what I feel and what does not seem right to me. Thank The trust built and impact had on our community families has laid the foundation for our schools to request our presence year after year. We have served our community for seven years now and have a waiting list of schools asking for our parenting seminars on their campus.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
